# 2. Python's basic characteristics

Python is:

| Characteristic               | Meaning                                            |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| High-level                   | Hides most machine-level details                   |
| General-purpose              | Can be used for many kinds of software             |
| Dynamically typed            | Variable types don't normally need to be declared  |
| Interpreted/runtime-executed | Python programs are executed by the Python runtime |
| Object-oriented              | Everything can be treated through objects          |
| Multi-paradigm               | Supports procedural, OOP, functional styles        |
| Garbage-collected            | Memory management is largely automatic             |
| Cross-platform               | Runs on Linux, Windows, macOS, etc.                |
| Open source                  | CPython and the language ecosystem are open source |
| Highly extensible            | Can integrate with C/C++ and other languages       |

One particularly important characteristic is **readability**.

