# 24. Python's weaknesses

Python is not ideal for everything.

### Performance

Python generally executes CPU-heavy code more slowly than C, C++, Rust, or Java.

### Dynamic typing

Dynamic typing provides flexibility but can allow certain errors to appear only at runtime.

### Memory consumption

Python objects can consume considerably more memory than equivalent low-level representations.

### Concurrency limitations in CPython

CPython has traditionally had the **Global Interpreter Lock (GIL)**, which affects execution of Python bytecode across threads for CPU-bound workloads. Modern Python has also introduced optional free-threaded builds, so this area is evolving.

### Mobile/browser development

Python isn't a mainstream choice for native mobile applications or browser frontend development.

